[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4377945624","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119248#issuecomment-4377945624","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119248","id":4377945624,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBPImGA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-05T09:14:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T09:17:39Z","body":"This seems like a documentation error, not an engine bug, the mesh used for this is not a 2D mesh, it's just a Sphere mesh so it doesn't \"exist\" in 2D, the code for navigation baking checks for the `ARRAY_FLAG_USE_2D_VERTICES` flag in the mesh\n\nThis is a natural limitation I'd say, as it's otherwise not trivial to know what the 2D extents of the mesh is, just projecting it onto a plane wouldn't necessarily be a viable solution\n\nWhile this might be improved in other ways I'd say this should be documented better\n\nEdit: This is [already documented](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_navigationpolygon.html#enum-navigationpolygon-parsedgeometrytype)\n> Meshes are only parsed when they use a 2D vertices surface format.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4377945624/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409800379","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119248#issuecomment-4409800379","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119248","id":4409800379,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBtg2uw","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T20:57:41Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T20:59:00Z","body":"Navigation can only parse what is valid 2d geometry.\nThose 3d meshes, apart from the most simple cases, are all broken geometry for 2d.\n\nThe issue here is that 2D itself has no actual 2D primitive meshes.\n\nMore than 8 years ago 2D started to use 3d primitives as a stopgap solution to have something.\nThat stopgap is by now close to lasting a decade in the engine.\n\nThe PR for actual dedicated Primitive2D meshes exists but is in limbo https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100574","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409800379/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5230567744","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119248#issuecomment-5230567744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119248","id":5230567744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN8QhQA","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T08:24:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T08:24:06Z","body":"> Meshes are only parsed when they use a 2D vertices surface format.\n\nClosing as this is mentioned in the parse settings of the NavigationPolygon.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url